// Converts a decimal string to a float.
// @retype storage only: float@EAX -> float@ST0, 2026-08-28. The TYPE was already correct and was NOT
// changed; only the return STORAGE was wrong.
// @evidence Both epilogues (00414916, 00414923) do FSTP float ptr [EBP+8]; FLD float ptr [EBP+8],
// leaving the narrowed result in ST(0), and the NULL path at 0041470f is FLDZ; RET 4. An x87 result is
// returned in ST(0), never in EAX. That explicit 4-byte round-trip is also the evidence that its twin
// SStrToDouble @004144c0, which has no such narrowing, returns a double.
